(Bug #27 regression: Repeat nested inside While, closed with two periods.
 The first period closes the Repeat, the second closes the While, so
 "after" runs once. Before the fix the Repeat did not consume its period,
 the second period had nothing to close, and the program failed with
 `Expected a statement, got Period`. The While runs twice (n: 0 then 1),
 each iteration prints r twice. Expected: r, r, r, r, after.)

a number called n is 0.
While n is less than 2,
    the n is n add 1,
    Repeat 2 times, Print "r"..
Print "after".